Z||000004||MrPBody||09-30-2001||06:36 PM||||You need a drill and/or chisel to remove some rivets.  Otherwise, just standard hand tools.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||grgoyl86||09-30-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>You need a drill and/or chisel to remove some rivets.  Otherwise, just standard hand tools.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I found that a hammer and puch works for most of the rivets. Use a punch with a slightly smaller diameter than the center of the rivets.<P>A T-15 Torx socket, along with 7mm, 10mm, 13mm, and 15mm sockets will remove a large part of the body. <P>Of course, a few screwdrivers and stuff like that, even a hacksaw for those REAL stubborn fasteners . . .<P>Last, but not least, bring a good supply of patience. It will really help at times . . .<P>Bob<BR>||||reg||12
